// ==============================================================================
// Aerix Standard Library: Window
// Native OS Windowing, Input Polling, Display Metrics, Clipboard, and GUI Engine
//
// Overview:
//   The Window module provides complete desktop GUI and OS window management
//   primitives for Windows. It integrates window lifecycle, modal message boxes,
//   global hardware input polling, display geometry inspection, system clipboard,
//   native controls (buttons, inputs, lists), and a high-performance 2D Canvas.
//
// Submodules:
//   - Window::Core      : MessageBox alerts, audio beeps, window handles (Z-order, title, minimize).
//   - Window::Metrics   : Screen resolutions, multi-monitor configuration, virtual desktop bounds.
//   - Window::Input     : Asynchronous keyboard polling (isKeyDown), virtual keys, mouse cursor positioning.
//   - Window::Clipboard : System clipboard text read, write, and clear operations.
//   - Window::Gui       : AppWindow lifecycle, controls (Button, TextBox, ListBox, ComboBox),
//                         dialogs, and the hardware-accelerated 2D Canvas drawing engine.
//
// Usage:
//   import "Window"
//
//   let win = AppWindow("Aerix App", 800, 600);
//   win.show();
//   while win.isOpen() {
//       win.poll();
//   }
// ==============================================================================

import "./core.arx"
import "./metrics.arx"
import "./input.arx"
import "./Clipboard/mod.arx"
import "./Gui/mod.arx"
